# Git Push & Commit

This is a personal / open-source repo. The machine has corporate tooling
installed globally (an `asd-cli` pre-commit / pre-push hook AND
`commit.gpgsign=true` with `gpg.format=x509` pointing at a corporate
x509 key) which fails on this repo with `no ssh cert is found`.

The user has explicitly authorized bypassing both. Always:

- **Commit:**

  ```bash
  git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit --no-verify -m "..."
  ```

- **Push:**

  ```bash
  git push --no-verify origin <branch>
  ```

Never run `ussh` or attempt to fix the corporate hook — just bypass it.

`origin/main` on https://github.com/kyberis/notetaker is wired to a
Vercel production deploy. Run `npm run lint && npx tsc --noEmit && npm
test && npm run build` before pushing to `main`. Production deploys run
`prisma:sync` automatically (gated by `VERCEL_ENV` in the build script);
preview deploys do not touch the database.
